      "verified_at": "2026-10-20T08:07:36.205Z",
      "notes": "Ume Sami (ISO 639-3: sju, Glottolog umes1235) is a critically endangered Sami language spoken mainly along the Ume River in present-day Arjeplog, Sorsele and Arvidsjaur, Sweden (Wikipedia). Of the 30 seeds, only 9 are in the documented Ume Sami area: Umea, Vannas, Robertsfors, Nordmaling, Bjurholm, Vindeln, Sorsele, Malå, Norsjo. The other 21 seeds are NOT in the Ume Sami area and/or are not settlements: Skolt, Sevettijarvi, Jukkasjarv, Gallivare, Kiruna, Jokkmokk (other Sami areas - North/Lule/Skolt Sami), Tromso, Vadsø, Nuorgam, Naatamo, Karesuando (North Sami, Norway/Finland), Kuusamo, Ivalo (Finland), Levitunturi, Kasivarsi, Halti, Korvatunturi, Ounasvaara, Pyhakero (fells/mountains, not settlements). Sele is ambiguous (Asele is on the Angerman river, not clearly Ume Sami). Since fewer than 25 seeds remain after removal, the entry cannot be verified. Seed list appears to be a generic Sami/Lapland list pasted in, not Ume Sami-specific toponyms."
